---
description: Resolve the actual intent-discovery goal through semantic composition and exact native authorities.
args:
  goal: string
returns: IntentReport
---
Resolve the actual local questions with the installed capability and observation codebases. Choose which current workspace, retained bytes, installed guide or live worker facts are needed; these are different kinds of evidence. Discovery and method descriptions identify real available operations, not observations of their results. Compose scoped investigation and conclusion, using exact owned coordinates for any native operation. Independent readonly observations may overlap; explicit requested order and real dependencies still matter.

Treat an unavailable method or missing result honestly. A saved note does not establish a running worker, an installed helper does not establish current workspace state, and permission to retain a private note is not a request. Retain only actual requested supported findings under native authority. Return the evidenced domain outcome and actual optional note, without fabricating observed scopes, method IDs or effects.
